=== entry 48e90b82cf46
kind: translation
rules: team-kit, verify-surface, loop, cursor-only
intent: Says `/deslop` is separate and may not be installed, how agents drive the app without control-ui and control-cli, and that timed repeats are T3 scheduled tasks; drops `/create-skill`. Keep the no-`/orchestrate` bullet.
--- upstream
- `/deslop`, `control-cli`, and `control-ui` ship in the `cursor-team-kit` plugin.
- `/loop` and `/create-skill` are Cursor built-ins.
- pstack has no `/orchestrate` skill. Orchestrate is a `/poteto-mode` playbook. If the slash menu shows `/orchestrate`, another plugin provides it.
--- patched
- `/deslop` ships separately, if it is installed. To drive the app, agents use the project's own verification skill, T3's `preview_*` tools for a UI, or the shell for a CLI.
- Repeating work on a timer uses T3's scheduled tasks (`schedule_task`), not a pstack skill.
- pstack has no `/orchestrate` skill. Orchestrate is a `/poteto-mode` playbook. If the slash menu shows `/orchestrate`, another plugin provides it.

=== entry a04779e1e9d9
kind: translation
rules: cursor-only, unshipped-link
intent: Says a playbook phrase without poteto-mode can start another installed skill, not Cursor's own, and drops the link to guide page 6, which isn't installed. No rule covers the first change exactly; closest faithful. Keep the pointer to the Playbooks section.
--- upstream
Without `/poteto-mode`, a phrase such as "babysit this pr" can start Cursor's own skill for the same job instead. The Playbooks section of [`poteto-mode`](../poteto-mode/SKILL.md) lists every playbook and when it applies. [Guide page 6](../../docs/guide/06-verify-and-ship.md) covers opening, babysitting, and landing a PR.
--- patched
Without `/poteto-mode`, a phrase such as "babysit this pr" can start another installed skill for the same job instead. The Playbooks section of [`poteto-mode`](../poteto-mode/SKILL.md) lists every playbook and when it applies.

=== entry 7d2da2886cde
kind: translation
rules: cursor-only
intent: Names T3's plan mode as what works alongside pstack. No rule covers Plan Mode; closest faithful. Keep the multi-phase plan and prototype routing.
--- upstream
pstack has no planning skill. Cursor's Plan Mode works alongside it. For work that spans phases or stacked PRs, asking `/poteto-mode` for a plan runs the [Multi-phase plan playbook](../poteto-mode/playbooks/multi-phase-plan.md), which writes the plan and doesn't implement it. For a design question, the Prototype playbook or `/architect` settles it in code first.
--- patched
pstack has no planning skill. T3's plan mode works alongside it. For work that spans phases or stacked PRs, asking `/poteto-mode` for a plan runs the [Multi-phase plan playbook](../poteto-mode/playbooks/multi-phase-plan.md), which writes the plan and doesn't implement it. For a design question, the Prototype playbook or `/architect` settles it in code first.

=== entry f33c24f37e47
kind: translation
rules: cursor-only, model-role, isolation, loop, unshipped-link
intent: Fix table without Custom Modes, cloud agents, the rule that applies to new chats, or the link to guide page 7 (not installed): the models file is read at each spawn, writers get their own worktree, and a loop until done needs a pass/fail check. Keep every symptom row.
--- upstream
| Symptom | Fix |
|---|---|
| The mode stopped applying after a few turns | It was started with Enter. Start it as a Custom Mode, or start each task with `/poteto-mode`. |
| A question got treated as the next step of the last task | Say "new task", or say the turn doesn't need the mode. |
| A new model choice had no effect | The rule from `/setup-pstack` applies to new chats. Start one. |
| Runs cost more than expected | See the cost paragraph under Get set up. |
| A skill didn't load on its own | Only `/setup-pstack` loads from the user's words. The others load when the user types them or when `/poteto-mode` runs them, and it doesn't run every skill. |
| Parallel agents overwrote each other | Give each agent its own worktree, or run them as cloud agents, which each get their own machine. |
| An overnight run moved but finished nothing | `/loop` needs a check that can pass or fail, not a duration. See [guide page 7](../../docs/guide/07-overnight.md). |
| The reply claims success from a green build | Ask for the real command, flow, stored value, or profile. That's the prove-it-works principle. |
--- patched
| Symptom | Fix |
|---|---|
| The mode stopped applying after a few turns | It was attached to one message and faded. Start each task with `/poteto-mode`. |
| A question got treated as the next step of the last task | Say "new task", or say the turn doesn't need the mode. |
| A new model choice had no effect | Skills read the models file `/setup-pstack` writes at each spawn. Check the role's line in it. |
| Runs cost more than expected | See the cost paragraph under Get set up. |
| A skill didn't load on its own | Only `/setup-pstack` loads from the user's words. The others load when the user types them or when `/poteto-mode` runs them, and it doesn't run every skill. |
| Parallel agents overwrote each other | Give each agent that writes its own worktree (`isolation: "worktree"`). |
| An overnight run moved but finished nothing | Looping until done needs a check that can pass or fail, not a duration. |
| The reply claims success from a green build | Ask for the real command, flow, stored value, or profile. That's the prove-it-works principle. |

