=== entry 56fa3df3e949
kind: translation
rules: paths, setup-pstack
intent: Install step says the skills go into the project's `.agents/skills/` with the `skills` CLI, and setup writes the project models file that skills read at each spawn. Keep the three steps and their order.
--- upstream
1. Install with `/add-plugin pstack` in chat, or from Customize in the sidebar.
2. Run [`/setup-pstack`](../setup-pstack/SKILL.md). It asks for a reasoning budget, maps a model to each role, and writes a rule. The rule applies to new chats.
3. Start a real task with `/poteto-mode`, a goal, and a check that can pass or fail.
--- patched
1. Install every pstack skill into the project's `.agents/skills/` with the `skills` CLI. They read each other, so take them all.
2. Run [`/setup-pstack`](../setup-pstack/SKILL.md). It asks for a reasoning budget, maps a model to each role, and writes {{snippet:models-file}}. Skills read it at each spawn.
3. Start a real task with `/poteto-mode`, a goal, and a check that can pass or fail.

=== entry 6073a15e97f2
kind: translation
rules: model-role
intent: Drops the `auto` alias and Cursor's Auto model; `inherit-parent` is the only alias. Keep the cost advice otherwise.
--- upstream
If cost is the worry, say where the tokens go and how to spend fewer. pstack spends extra tokens on subagents and review panels. Rerun `/setup-pstack` and pick a smaller budget or cheaper models. A role set to `auto` or `inherit-parent` runs on the chat's model, which saves tokens when the chat runs on Auto or a cheaper model. A shorter panel list runs fewer subagents, one for each entry. Save `/poteto-mode` for work that needs rigor.
--- patched
If cost is the worry, say where the tokens go and how to spend fewer. pstack spends extra tokens on subagents and review panels. Rerun `/setup-pstack` and pick a smaller budget or cheaper models. A role set to `inherit-parent` runs on the chat's model, which saves tokens when the chat runs on a cheaper model. A shorter panel list runs fewer subagents, one for each entry. Save `/poteto-mode` for work that needs rigor.

=== entry 7ef3ed2d9c2e
kind: translation
rules: unshipped-link
intent: Drops the sentence pointing at pstack's README and guide page 1, which aren't installed. Keep that installing changes nothing until a skill is invoked, that only `/setup-pstack` loads on its own, and the offer to word the first prompt.
